\unmutenow unmutes one or more instruments immediately.
Its syntax is the following:

\unmutenow \violin \cello

where \violin and \cello are instruments created with
\insts.init. To unmute all instruments, call:

\unmutenow \all

Unlike \unmute, which waits for the start of the next bar,
\unmutenow unmutes the instruments at once, even in the
middle of a bar.

\unmutenow needs at least one argument, and an argument
that is not an instrument results in an "unknown
instrument" error.
